## Waker — handle a Future stashes to notify the executor when it
## becomes pollable again. Two methods: `wake` (consumes the waker)
## and `wake_by_ref` (borrowed).
##
## Sub-phase 3 of the async round (executor.spec.md B3): both
## methods are no-ops. The poll loop in block_on spins
## continuously (with Thread.yield_now between iterations), so any
## "wake" is implicit. Sub-phase 4 wires real signaling when async
## I/O introduces genuine blocking park points.
class Waker
  lib "runtime/executor.c"
    def wake as "ruxen_waker_wake" -> nil
    def wake_by_ref as "ruxen_waker_wake_by_ref" -> nil
  end
end

## --- Sub-phase 4A: reactor free-fn lib decls -----------------------
##
## Spec: docs/specs/stdlib/async_io.spec.md Milestone 4A.
##
## The reactor primitives in C (runtime/reactor.c) are declared here
## as free-fn lib decls so `TimeSleepFuture` and the step-future
## helpers (step_future.rx, used by async_net / async_fs / async_io)
## reach them through the FFI alias map.
##
## 4A landed in two steps. Commit `42daaeb` shipped the C reactor +
## per-thread lifecycle (Context.executor / Context.drop) + the
## `Thread.yield_now` → `ruxen_reactor_park_current` indirection.
## The user-side Async.sleep / TimeSleepFuture follow here.
lib "runtime/reactor.c"
  def ruxen_reactor_current_handle -> Int
  def ruxen_reactor_register_timer(reactor: Int, nanos: Int) -> Int
  def ruxen_reactor_set_waker(reactor: Int, handle: Int, waker: &Waker) -> nil
  def ruxen_reactor_check_fired(reactor: Int, handle: Int) -> Int
  def ruxen_reactor_deregister(reactor: Int, handle: Int) -> nil
  def ruxen_reactor_register_fd_read(reactor: Int, fd: Int) -> Int
  def ruxen_reactor_register_fd_write(reactor: Int, fd: Int) -> Int
end

## `ruxen_reactor_rearm_timer` (Lever D.2, same C file) is deliberately NOT
## declared here: it is called ONLY C-to-C, from
## async_net.c::ruxen_async_tcp_stream_ensure_timer, mirroring
## `ruxen_reactor_register_fd_read_persistent`/`_write_persistent` and
## `ruxen_reactor_next_virtual_deadline` (also reactor.c primitives with zero
## `.rx` lib decl — the latter is used only by test_clock.c). No `.rx` caller
## needs it, so it stays off the FFI alias-map surface rather than adding an
## unused declaration.

## Monotonic nanos free fn used by `TimeSleepFuture` to compute its
## absolute deadline. Cross-package lib decl pointing at the C symbol
## owned by std.time's runtime/time.c.
lib "../../time/runtime/time.c"
  def ruxen_time_now_ns -> Int
end
